                      (    forth6809.asm):06937         ; wraparound, not tested here - see TSTDOLP's own notes). This
                      (    forth6809.asm):06938         ; case IS fast and safe to test directly: QDOSETUP's own skip
                      (    forth6809.asm):06939         ; check happens before the loop is entered at all, confirmed by
                      (    forth6809.asm):06940         ; hand-trace of its code. Same "?DO I + LOOP" body, but since
                      (    forth6809.asm):06941         ; the body never runs, the seed should come back completely
                      (    forth6809.asm):06942         ; unchanged (0, not 10).
                      (    forth6809.asm):06943         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
