                      (    forth6809.asm):08200         ; TSTCRDOES - unit test for CREATE/DOES> together. Compiles the
                      (    forth6809.asm):08201         ; equivalent of "CREATE TESTWD 5 , DOES> @ 1+" directly (CREATE,
                      (    forth6809.asm):08202         ; store 5 at the PFA, DOES>'s own compile action, then @ and 1+
                      (    forth6809.asm):08203         ; compiled as the new behavior, terminated with RTS) - executing
                      (    forth6809.asm):08204         ; TESTWD should push 6 (5 fetched, then incremented).
                      (    forth6809.asm):08205         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):08206         ; DOES>'s own runtime action (SETDOES) does a documented "double
                      (    forth6809.asm):08207         ; return": it patches LATEST's behavior field using the return
                      (    forth6809.asm):08208         ; address ITS OWN "JSR SETDOES" call provides, then pops a
                      (    forth6809.asm):08209         ; SECOND return address and jumps there - designed for the
                      (    forth6809.asm):08210         ; normal case where DOES> is reached from inside an enclosing
                      (    forth6809.asm):08211         ; defining word (like a real ": MAKETEST CREATE ... DOES> ... ;"
                      (    forth6809.asm):08212         ; would compile), which itself has its own caller. Traced by
                      (    forth6809.asm):08213         ; hand: calling directly into the compiled "JSR SETDOES"
                      (    forth6809.asm):08214         ; instruction itself (not through an intermediate wrapper)
                      (    forth6809.asm):08215         ; naturally supplies exactly the two stack levels SETDOES
                      (    forth6809.asm):08216         ; expects - its own JSR provides the first (becoming the new
                      (    forth6809.asm):08217         ; behavior field value), and this test's own call provides the
                      (    forth6809.asm):08218         ; second (correctly resuming here afterward) - no extra
                      (    forth6809.asm):08219         ; scaffolding needed, confirmed correct rather than assumed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):08220         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
