                      (    forth6809.asm):09106         ; TSTISOF - unit test for IS and ACTION-OF together. Compiles
                      (    forth6809.asm):09107         ; "DEFER TESTWD", interprets "DUP IS TESTWD" directly (IS parses
                      (    forth6809.asm):09108         ; "TESTWD" via WORD+FIND, needing LATEST still pointed at it -
                      (    forth6809.asm):09109         ; not restored until this whole test finishes), executes TESTWD
                      (    forth6809.asm):09110         ; (should now behave like DUP), then interprets "ACTION-OF
                      (    forth6809.asm):09111         ; TESTWD" to fetch the current target by name and confirms it
                      (    forth6809.asm):09112         ; matches DUP's own xt. Explicitly forces STATE=0 before both IS
                      (    forth6809.asm):09113         ; and ACTION-OF, since both are documented to behave differently
                      (    forth6809.asm):09114         ; by STATE, same reasoning as TSTVALTO's own TO test.
                      (    forth6809.asm):09115         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
