                      (    forth6809.asm):09477         ; TSTCOMPWORDS - compiling-words tests (glossary section 3.10,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09478         ; 13 words, 17 tests since several get separate cases: TICK
                      (    forth6809.asm):09479         ; found/not-found, ['] compiling/interpreting state, POSTPONE
                      (    forth6809.asm):09480         ; normal/immediate word, SLITERAL compiling/interpreting state,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09481         ; ABORT" false/true flag). Reuses the scratch infrastructure
                      (    forth6809.asm):09482         ; established for sections 3.8/3.9 throughout.
                      (    forth6809.asm):09483         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):09484         ; POSTPONE is this section's hardest case: a genuine two-level
                      (    forth6809.asm):09485         ; compile-time mechanism. Traced its own code first - for a
                      (    forth6809.asm):09486         ; normal word, it compiles code that ITSELF compiles a call to
                      (    forth6809.asm):09487         ; that word later, when the current definition eventually runs,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09488         ; not immediately (standard ANS semantics: POSTPONE appends a
                      (    forth6809.asm):09489         ; word's own compilation semantics to the current definition,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09490         ; and for an ordinary word that semantics IS "compile a call to
                      (    forth6809.asm):09491         ; it", so appending it only makes sense if the current
                      (    forth6809.asm):09492         ; definition later performs that compiling action itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):09493         ; against whatever's being compiled at that later point).
                      (    forth6809.asm):09494         ; Verified via the compiled byte sequence directly rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):09495         ; fully executing a triple-nested compile chain.
                      (    forth6809.asm):09496         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):09497         ; ABORT" is safely testable for both its flag cases - confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):09498         ; by reading its own runtime code that it uses THROW -2
                      (    forth6809.asm):09499         ; internally, not the raw, never-returns ABORT mechanism plain
                      (    forth6809.asm):09500         ; ABORT itself uses (still deliberately untested, per section
                      (    forth6809.asm):09501         ; 3.1's own reasoning).
                      (    forth6809.asm):09502         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
