                      (    forth6809.asm):12097         ; Strings & Parsing test harness (glossary section 3.12). Reuses
                      (    forth6809.asm):12098         ; the redirect infrastructure from sections 3.8-3.10 for the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12099         ; name-parsing words (WORD/CHAR/[CHAR]/S"/."). DOTQUOTE's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):12100         ; runtime (DOTSTR) calls TYPE internally, which - per section
                      (    forth6809.asm):12101         ; 3.1's own already-debugged finding - has two entirely
                      (    forth6809.asm):12102         ; different implementations gated by SERIALPOLL; its own test
                      (    forth6809.asm):12103         ; below applies that same lesson from the start rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):12104         ; re-discovering it.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12105         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12106         ; SUBSTITUTE/REPLACES/UNESCAPE all have extensive prior-session
                      (    forth6809.asm):12107         ; bug-fix history baked into their own comments (SUBSTITUTE's
                      (    forth6809.asm):12108         ; %-delimiter algorithm, UNESCAPE's doubling-not-escaping
                      (    forth6809.asm):12109         ; behavior) - trusted as ground truth here (each confirmed via a
                      (    forth6809.asm):12110         ; prior MAME-tested session), verified fresh against the actual
                      (    forth6809.asm):12111         ; code rather than re-derived from scratch, and tested against
                      (    forth6809.asm):12112         ; that confirmed, current behavior.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12113         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):12114         
                      (    forth6809.asm):12115         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
