                      (    forth6809.asm):20996         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):20997         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):20998         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):20999         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):21000         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):21001         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):21002         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):21003         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):21004         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):21005         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):21006         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):21007         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):21008         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):21009         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):21010         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):21011         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):21012         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):21013         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):21014         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):21015         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):21016         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):21017         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
